<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 25 January, from 1533 to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1533</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII secretly marries Anne Boleyn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry married the pregnant Anne Boleyn in a private ceremony at Whitehall while still married to Catherine of Aragon. To make the marriage lawful he broke with Rome and headed his own Church of England.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1554</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jesuit missionaries found São Paulo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Manuel da Nóbrega and José de Anchieta celebrated Mass at a new Jesuit mission on the Piratininga plateau. The settlement grew into São Paulo, now the largest city in the Southern Hemisphere.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1858</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria's eldest daughter marries Prince Frederick of Prussia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Victoria, the Princess Royal, married the future German Emperor Frederick III at St James's Palace. Mendelssohn's 'Wedding March' played as they left, starting a fashion for it at weddings.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1881</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edison and Bell interests form the Oriental Telephone Company</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Companies holding the telephone patents of Thomas Edison and Alexander Graham Bell combined to form the Oriental Telephone Company. It built early telephone exchanges in India and other parts of Asia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell">Alexander Graham Bell</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1924</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Winter Olympics open at Chamonix</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An 'International Winter Sports Week' opened at Chamonix in the French Alps with athletes from 16 nations. The International Olympic Committee later recognised it as the first Winter Olympic Games.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1945</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of the Bulge ends in Allied victory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Allied forces restored their line in the Ardennes, ending Germany's last major offensive in the west. Fought in bitter winter conditions, it was the costliest American battle of the Second World War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1971</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Idi Amin seizes power in Uganda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">While President Milton Obote was abroad, army commander Idi Amin took power in a coup. His eight-year rule saw the expulsion of Uganda's Asians and the killing of an estimated 100,000 to 500,000 people.</p></li></ol>
